From c93678aa038656a782274da34b06f22a5638a633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:04:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(sinker): generate an electrode from a cavity's
 picked faces

A sinker EDM electrode is derived from the picked faces of a part's
cavity - its level floor and every vertical wall standing on it - and
added as #541's electrode tool in one undo step.

- motion::sinker_cavity reads a face set as one cavity: each face
  checked on its own (finite, in range, planar, non-zero area, closed),
  the walls matched to the floor's outer ring edge by edge, every floor
  edge covered end to end. Anything else is refused by name.
- motion::sinker_electrode offsets the outline inward by undersize +
  orbit (geo2d's Clipper2 offset, cross-checked against the arithmetic)
  and extends it a stated stub above the cavity's mouth. The stock sim's
  box atom burns a rectangular face only, so a cavity that is not an
  axis-aligned rectangle is refused by name (#1152 owns the body
  electrode). A boss, rib or overhang in the cavity's column refuses
  the electrode with the spot.
- app: operation::sinker_faces resolves the picks (the one pick rule,
  outward normals by winding) and reads a condition's undersize by id;
  commands::ElectrodeFromFaces is the undoable command; MCP
  electrode_from_faces runs it and answers with the Sinker Burn's
  numbers.

Pinned by motion's sinker_electrode_tests and sinker_electrode_fuzz
(seeded: 6000 damaged cavities refused by name, 20000 garbage face
sets) and app's sinker_electrode / sinker_electrode_mcp (the generated
rough and finish electrodes burn the pocket clean in the program
verdict). Synthetic conditions only; not exercised on a real EDM
control.

Fixes #547

